{
  "_comment": [
    "MARA: 'unbiased' is not a property a news source has. What you can build is:",
    "  (1) PRIMARY sources - the Fed, BLS, Treasury, SEC. These publish numbers,",
    "      not narrative. Weight them first, always.",
    "  (2) A SPREAD of press across leans. You are not filtering for truth, you",
    "      are making disagreement visible. lean= is a label for the reader, not",
    "      a score. Where left/center/right report the same fact, that fact is",
    "      probably solid. Where they diverge, that IS the interesting signal.",
    "Run `python3 scripts/doctor.py` to see which of these are actually alive.",
    "Feeds die constantly - Reuters and AP both retired public RSS. Delete dead",
    "ones rather than letting them fail silently every 30 minutes.",
    "filter:true = a GENERAL news feed. Items must match a keywords_important term to be stored. Added after the first live run filled the rail with an Ebola outbreak and a football transfer."
  ],
